# matrix.env — MATRIX runtime tuning parameters.
#
# RECON-W30. This file exists so that no tuning number lives inside a shell script.
# A magic number in start-mind.sh is a value that cannot be changed for another machine
# without editing code, which means it will not be changed, which means it is not a
# tuning parameter at all — it is a constant that has forgotten it was once a decision.
#
# scripts/start-mind.sh sources this file. Every variable below can be overridden by the
# caller's environment, so a deployment profile is "MATRIX_ENV_FILE=... start-mind.sh",
# not a patch.
#
# Provenance: every value cites where it came from and whether it was MEASURED or
# DERIVED. See docs-v2/operations/TUNING-PARAMETERS.md for the derivations and the
# measurements. Do not add a value here without adding its provenance there; an
# untraceable tuning parameter is worse than no tuning parameter.
#
# Machine this was derived for (see HARDWARE-PROFILE.md):
#   AMD Ryzen 9 9955HX, 16 physical cores / 32 logical, AVX-512 (no AMX),
#   59.5 GiB RAM, single NUMA node.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# JVM
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Heap: 50% of 59.5 GiB, sized equal to Xms so the heap never resizes mid-run.
# DERIVED from MemTotal. A JVM that owns nearly all RAM evicts the page cache the
# NVMe tier depends on, and NVMe latency is ~2 orders of magnitude worse than L3.
# @see TUNING-PARAMETERS.md §3
MATRIX_HEAP="${MATRIX_HEAP:-16g}"

# ZGC over G1 for sub-millisecond pauses, so a long sleep cycle cannot stall the
# gateway. The throughput difference between them was NOT significant (error bars
# overlapped on both workloads); the decision rests on documented pause behaviour,
# not on a win this project measured. Flip to -XX:+UseG1GC to compare.
# @see TUNING-PARAMETERS.md §5 — this is the value most likely to be overturned
MATRIX_GC="${MATRIX_GC:--XX:+UseZGC}"

# The Vector API is an incubating module and is not resolved by default. The HDC
# kernels use it. Required by the build as well as the runtime.
MATRIX_JVM_MODULES="${MATRIX_JVM_MODULES:---add-modules=jdk.incubator.vector}"

# JMX/management. Left off by default: an internet-facing deployment should not
# expose an unauthenticated management port, and enabling it "just for debugging"
# is how that happens.
MATRIX_JMX="${MATRIX_JMX:-false}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Concurrency
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Physical cores, not the 32 logical CPUs. SMT siblings share L1d, L2 and the vector
# units, so oversubscribing them trades cache residency for throughput that is not
# there. DERIVED from lscpu.
# @see TUNING-PARAMETERS.md §2 — a CEILING, not a tuned value; no MATRIX workload
# here is parallel enough to saturate a pool.
MATRIX_WORKER_THREADS="${MATRIX_WORKER_THREADS:-16}"

# NDJSON appends and SQLite writes block on the NVMe tier, not the CPU, so this
# tracks the worker count rather than exceeding it.
MATRIX_IO_THREADS="${MATRIX_IO_THREADS:-16}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Batching
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Distillation chunk: sized so one chunk's working set stays in the 1 MiB L2 slice a
# single core owns (16 MiB L2 / 16 cores). 8192 records of a 1024-bit code is on the
# order of that. DERIVED from a cache-occupancy argument — no sweep has measured
# chunk size against throughput yet.
# @see TUNING-PARAMETERS.md §4
MATRIX_DISTILL_CHUNK="${MATRIX_DISTILL_CHUNK:-8192}"

# Replay batch for the hippocampal scheduler.
MATRIX_REPLAY_BATCH="${MATRIX_REPLAY_BATCH:-256}"

# Tsetlin clause batch. A power of two so the clause-chunk index is a shift, not a
# divide, in the hot update loop.
MATRIX_CLAUSE_BATCH="${MATRIX_CLAUSE_BATCH:-4096}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ports
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Gateway. Prompts override MATRIX_PORT (8799 for smoke, 8774/8775 for federation)
# and these defaults follow, which is why the health check must read the variable
# rather than hardcoding a port.
MATRIX_PORT="${MATRIX_PORT:-8765}"
MATRIX_PROMETHEUS_PORT="${MATRIX_PROMETHEUS_PORT:-9094}"
MATRIX_WEB_PORT="${MATRIX_WEB_PORT:-3050}"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HDC
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Sparse-HDC code width used by EpisodeFeatureExtractor. 1024 bits = 128 bytes per
# code, which fits a 1024-bit vector in 16 AVX-512 lanes.
#
# NOTE: the measured 2.98x win for a long[] encoding over the BitSet clone path is
# recorded in TUNING-PARAMETERS.md §6 and deliberately NOT applied — changing the
# storage encoding is a schema migration, and Article VIII forbids keeping a parallel
# long[] store in sync with the BitSet one as shadow logic.
MATRIX_HDC_DIMENSION="${MATRIX_HDC_DIMENSION:-1024}"

# Winner-take-all sparsity K: bits active per token.
MATRIX_HDC_K="${MATRIX_HDC_K:-64}"
